# Grill-me / Hardening Gate

**Phase 1 only.** Do not write implementation code during this phase.

Before coding, challenge the request once:

- Exact scope and explicit out-of-scope
- Likely files/modules and architecture layer
- Tests and verification gates that prove completion
- Destructive or irreversible operations (dry-run, user approval)
- Merge target: commit-only, PR, or merge — and branch/base
- Dominant specs/plans under `docs/superpowers/` when applicable

## Output (single pass)

- Assumptions
- Risks
- Proposed implementation sequence (numbered tasks)
- Stop conditions (true blockers per always-on core rule)
- Verification gates per phase

Ask the user for approval **once**. Do not ask between future tasks.

## After approval

- Scope is **locked** — no re-scoping without explicit user message.
- User attaches mission-execution rule and confirms autonomous run (see rules index in `00-core.mdc`).
- No persona roleplay unless the user opts in.

**Inactive for:** small one-file fixes, typos, lint-only, read-only Q&A, docs-only edits.
